==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|ar}} {{Arab|[[حسن|حَسَن]]}} meaning fine, good, good-looking, handsome, manly or strong.

====Proper noun====
{{wikipedia|Hasan bin Ali}}
'''Hassan''' or '''Hasan'''

# {{Islam}} The first son of [[Ali]] and brother of [[Husein]]; the second [[Shiite]] [[Imam]].
# {{given name|male|from=Arabic}} used by [[Muslim]]s.

=====Usage notes=====
The name Hassan in [[Hebrew]] '''חסן''' means "cantor", or "good cantor" derived from the Arabic "good" and the Hebrew "cantor"

